Subject: Re: FinApps — Tool calling integration post-call recap

Quick engineering notes from our side:

- SDK setup: we’ll provide a sample repo with platform-agnostic wrappers (Node + Python) that include: auth adapters, retry middleware, and a tools manifest loader.
- Routing: recommend a simple policy config (region vs latency vs cost) and a model-fallback list. Example: [gpt-redwood-medium, gpt-redwood-small].
- Batching: enable continuous batching for chat-like flows to improve throughput — sample config will be in the repo.

Sample Node snippet for tool call (sync orchestration/fan-out):

// pseudocode
const tools = loadToolsManifest('./tools.json');
const results = await Promise.all([
  callTool('fraud_score', payload),
  callTool('enrichment', payload),
  callTool('embeddings_lookup', payload)
]);
const aggregated = aggregateResults(results);

// handle partial failures
if (aggregated.missingCritical) {
  // fall back to cached data or ask user confirmation
}

I’ll drop the sample repo link in the architecture call invite. Also happy to walk through the tool schema during the call.

—Ben
Senior Engineer, Redwood Inference

